Adaptation (internal/gateway legacy /v1/completions sampling carriers): no
upstream code is adapted; the contract is inspired by the finding. Upstream
builds every request's SamplingParams from the client's non-null fields
(llm_engine.py:526), binds a per-sequence seed (sampling_params.py:61,74,86-91)
and refuses out-of-range values with an error rather than serving a request
that ignored them (sampling_params.py:93-105), apart from logprobs, which it
drops without a word (sampling_params.py:63). It has no HTTP completions wire
and no frequency/presence penalties, logit_bias or min_p. Fak's legacy
/v1/completions route had silently dropped seed, logit_bias,
frequency_penalty, presence_penalty, top_k and min_p. It now decodes them with
/v1/chat/completions' types, refuses an out-of-range penalty with chat's typed
400 (sampling_param_out_of_range) before admission and before any EP follower
or stream preamble, and passes all six to the planner with chat's options, so
ride upstreams receive them and native or provider refusals carry chat's
codes. A seeded stream:true opens its SSE stream after the decode, as chat
does, so an unsupported seed is an HTTP 400 sampling_seed_unsupported rather
than an in-band stream error.
